@startuml

title PENA POC 01 — Runtime Pipeline Design

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #2F5597
  BackgroundColor #F8FBFF
  ArrowColor #444444
}

skinparam note {
  BorderColor #666666
  BackgroundColor #FFFCE8
}

start

:Start POC run;
:Load runtime configuration;
:Load repository context;
:Load prompt templates;
:Load local article inputs;

if (Inputs valid?) then (yes)
  :Normalize article records;
  :Attach source metadata;
  :Deduplicate repeated content;
  :Apply trust scoring;
  :Apply relevance scoring;
  :Build LLM summarization prompts;
  :Call LLM provider;
  :Validate structured summary response;
  :Generate markdown digest;
  :Write digest artifact;
  :Write observability report;
  :Write run log;

  if (Human feedback captured?) then (yes)
    :Create learning note;
    :Store learning candidate;
  else (no)
    :Mark run as unreviewed;
  endif

  :Prepare next-iteration inputs;

else (no)
  :Write validation error report;
  :Stop run safely;
endif

stop

note right
This is the first executable POC flow.

It should be implemented as a small,
observable, local-first CLI pipeline.
end note

note bottom
The runtime pipeline turns the low-level design
into an implementation-ready execution contract.
end note

@enduml
